  drop shadow) was triggering on ANY viewport >=640px wide -- which
  wrongly caught large Android phones, phablets, tablets, and even a
  regular phone rotated to landscape. Gated it behind (pointer:fine)
  so it only shows on mouse/trackpad desktop browsers; any real
  touchscreen now gets a native full-bleed layout at every width
- Desktop mockup height now clamps to min(860px, 94vh) so it can't
  overflow/clip on short browser windows
- Added safe-area-inset-top handling for the app bar on real devices
  (notch/status bar), matching the existing bottom safe-area handling
- Added a <360px breakpoint tightening padding, font sizes, and
  segmented control sizing for small phones (iPhone SE etc.)
- Added a short-viewport (<=560px height) breakpoint for landscape
  phones/small windows -- trims vertical rhythm and hides the
  subtitle line so the whole card fits without excess scrolling
- Verified: all 6 reference QR codes still match exactly, and
  overflow/boundary/empty-input logic is unaffected (CSS-only change)
